From 947b907a71e6b3015d94d8b52691d63a34b7b641 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:50:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(motion): keep the custom-limit refusal, pin the
 trochoidal clean-up check

Review fixes for PR #4008 (head b05f1318c):

1. Restore main's whole-path refusal for a custom max_engagement. The
   clean-up check only steps the peel down first. Decision in
   docs/decisions/3849-trochoidal-cleanup-engagement.md.
2. No expect() or unchecked index in the clean-up check: the baseline is
   a plain value, the first chain point is read with first().
3. End-to-end pins: a 2D and a 3D Trochoidal operation on a notch pocket
   carry Warning::EngagementExceeded in the cached warnings.
4. Step-down pins: wide 30x24 D6 and L-shape D10 at 60 deg step down,
   post, carry the "peel step was reduced" note and no warning.
5. A pin that is red on upstream/main: the notch pocket at the 90 deg
   default (118.5 deg on main, no note). The test comment is corrected.
6. The warning names the clean-up feed through the measured peak (the
   note carries the level Z), not the first lane cut.

The check and its notes move to adaptive_troch_check.rs (400-line rule).

Refs #3849

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
